From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ime: type any single character on its real key when the layout has it

Steam's on-screen keyboard types through gamescope's input method. A single
character is typed on its real key only when it is one byte, so every
accented letter took the remapped-keycode path: gamescope maps a spare key
(1, 2, ...) to the character for a moment and presses it. Clients that read
keysyms get the character, but clients that forward the physical key, like
a Moonlight stream to Windows, send that spare key: an Italian keyboard
types 1 for è, à, ò, ù.

Decode the whole character before looking for it in the layout, and allow
AltGr (Mod5) as well, so with XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT matching the host the
letters and symbols (@ #) go out on their real keys.

---
diff --git a/src/ime.cpp b/src/ime.cpp
index 518ac02..8d57ffd 100644
--- a/src/ime.cpp
+++ b/src/ime.cpp
@@ -342,7 +342,8 @@ static bool try_type_keysym(struct wlserver_input_method *ime, xkb_keysym_t keys
 					continue;
 				}
 
-				xkb_mod_mask_t allowed = WLR_MODIFIER_SHIFT | WLR_MODIFIER_CTRL | WLR_MODIFIER_ALT;
+				// AltGr (Mod5) too: @ # and the euro sign on many layouts
+				xkb_mod_mask_t allowed = WLR_MODIFIER_SHIFT | WLR_MODIFIER_CTRL | WLR_MODIFIER_ALT | WLR_MODIFIER_MOD5;
 				if ((mask & allowed) != mask) {
 					continue;
 				}
@@ -367,11 +368,18 @@ static bool try_type_keysym(struct wlserver_input_method *ime, xkb_keysym_t keys
 void type_text(struct wlserver_input_method *ime, const char *text)
 {
 	// If possible, try to type the character without switching the keymap
-	// ...unless we're already using a fancy keymap
-	if (utf8_size(text) == 1 && text[1] == '\0' && ime->keys.empty()) {
-		xkb_keysym_t keysym = keysym_from_ch(text[0]);
-		if (keysym != XKB_KEY_NoSymbol && try_type_keysym(ime, keysym)) {
-			return;
+	// ...unless we're already using a fancy keymap. Any single character, not
+	// only ASCII: with a matching layout (XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT) an accented
+	// letter is a real key, and clients that forward physical keys (game
+	// streaming) only get it right that way.
+	if (ime->keys.empty()) {
+		const char *rest = text;
+		uint32_t ch = utf8_decode(&rest);
+		if (ch != UTF8_INVALID && rest[0] == '\0') {
+			xkb_keysym_t keysym = keysym_from_ch(ch);
+			if (keysym != XKB_KEY_NoSymbol && try_type_keysym(ime, keysym)) {
+				return;
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
